<section class="ls-hero"><div class="ls-w ls-hero-g"><div class="ls-hero-t"><p class="ls-script">la nostra cucina</p><h1>Every layer<br><span>matters.</span></h1><p class="ls-lead">A kitchen guide to lasagna: how much pasta and sauce your pan needs, how to build clean layers, and how to bake, freeze and reheat it so every slice stands tall.</p><div class="ls-hero-a"><a class="ls-btn" href="#calc">Plan my pan</a><a class="ls-btn ls-btn-o" href="#bake">Bake &amp; reheat</a></div>
<ul class="ls-hero-k"><li><b data-count="3">0</b>hours to make, start to finish</li><li><b data-count="15">0</b>minutes to rest before slicing</li><li><b data-count="12">0</b>servings from a 9&times;13 pan</li></ul></div>
<div class="ls-hero-v"><figure class="ls-plate"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1762631883229-95cfb6a063ad?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=560&q=75" alt="a slice of lasagna with melted cheese" width="560" height="560" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="ls-stack" aria-hidden="true"><div class="ls-steam"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><div class="ls-dish"><i class="l-pasta" style="--i:0"></i><i class="l-ragu" style="--i:1"></i><i class="l-bech" style="--i:2"></i><i class="l-pasta" style="--i:3"></i><i class="l-ragu" style="--i:4"></i><i class="l-bech" style="--i:5"></i><i class="l-pasta" style="--i:6"></i><i class="l-top" style="--i:7"></i></div><div class="ls-pan"></div></div><p class="ls-note">fresh from the oven!</p></div></div></section>

<section class="ls-ing"><div class="ls-w"><div class="ls-ing-h"><p class="ls-script">what goes in</p><h2 class="rv">Four building blocks</h2></div><ul class="ls-ing-l stg"><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792354054692-8c9a69e84ed5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="a sheet of fresh pasta dough" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><div><b>Pasta</b><p>Fresh or dried sheets. No-boil sheets save a step.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1757920337591-02aa3c80cabc?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="chopped tomatoes and onions cooking in a pan" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><div><b>Ragù</b><p>A slow tomato and meat sauce, or vegetables.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574175679306-4c5f33146b6f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="a person grating cheese" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><div><b>Cheese</b><p>Mozzarella to melt, parmesan for flavour.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1777205838206-03e7248e474c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="basil plants growing in pots" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><div><b>Basil</b><p>A few torn leaves on top, just before serving.</p></div></li></ul></div></section>

<section class="ls-s ls-calc" id="calc"><div class="ls-w"><div class="ls-sh"><p class="ls-script">tool one</p><h2 class="rv">Pan &amp; layer calculator</h2><p class="ls-p">Pick your pan and how many layers you like. The cross-section and shopping amounts update as you go.</p></div>
<div class="ls-calc-g"><div class="ls-calc-c"><p class="ls-lb">Pan size</p><div class="ls-pans" id="pc-p" role="group" aria-label="Pan size"><button type="button" data-v="8x8">8 &times; 8 in square</button><button type="button" data-v="9x13" class="on">9 &times; 13 in classic</button><button type="button" data-v="10x15">10 &times; 15 in large</button><button type="button" data-v="12x17">12 &times; 17 in half sheet</button></div><label class="ls-lb" for="pc-l">Pasta layers: <b id="pc-lv">4</b></label><input type="range" id="pc-l" min="3" max="6" value="4" class="ls-rng">
<p class="ls-lb">Sauce</p><div class="ls-seg" id="pc-s" role="group" aria-label="Sauce style"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on">Meat ragù</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Vegetable</button></div>
<div class="ls-xs" id="pc-x" aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
<div class="ls-card" aria-live="polite"><div class="ls-card-h"><span>Shopping list</span><b id="pc-sv">12 servings</b></div><ul class="ls-list"><li><span>Lasagna sheets</span><b id="pc-a"></b></li><li><span id="pc-sn">Ragù</span><b id="pc-b"></b></li><li><span>Béchamel</span><b id="pc-c"></b></li><li><span>Mozzarella</span><b id="pc-d"></b></li><li><span>Parmesan</span><b id="pc-e"></b></li></ul><p class="ls-small">Amounts are a guide for dried sheets. Fresh sheets cover a little more each.</p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="ls-s ls-bake" id="bake"><div class="ls-w ls-bake-g"><div><p class="ls-script">tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Bake &amp; reheat planner</h2><p class="ls-p">Fresh from assembly, chilled overnight or straight from the freezer: each needs a different bake. Choose where yours is starting.</p>
<div class="ls-start" id="bk-s" role="group" aria-label="Starting point"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on"><b>Fresh</b><span>Just assembled</span></button><button type="button" data-v="1"><b>Chilled</b><span>From the fridge</span></button><button type="button" data-v="2"><b>Frozen</b><span>From the freezer</span></button><button type="button" data-v="3"><b>Leftover</b><span>A single slice</span></button></div>
<label class="ls-lb" for="bk-t">Ready to eat at</label><input type="time" id="bk-t" value="19:00" class="ls-in"></div>
<div class="ls-tl-w"><div class="ls-oven" aria-hidden="true"><div class="ls-oven-d"><div class="ls-oven-g"></div></div><div class="ls-oven-k"><i></i><i></i></div><b id="bk-o">375&deg;F</b></div><ol class="ls-tl" id="bk-l" aria-live="polite"></ol></div></div></section>

<section class="ls-gal"><div class="ls-w ls-gal-g"><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792354441702-572e1ffaca2b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=500&h=360&q=75" alt="a glass dish of golden baked lasagna" width="500" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1770908811367-e1232962e81b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="a slice of lasagna being served from a baking dish" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1767065583952-e932c354bca6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="cheesy lasagna lifted on a fork" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="ls-gal-t rv"><p class="ls-script">the golden rule</p><p class="ls-q">Let it rest for fifteen minutes. The layers settle, and every slice comes out clean.</p></div></div></section>

